Given that $1000 compounds annually at a constant interest rate $r$, after three years, the amount $A$ is given by $A = 1000\left(1 + \frac{r}{100}\right)^3.$  We can substitute $A=1225$ and solve for $r$:

\begin{align*}
1225&amp;=1000\left(1 + \frac{r}{100}\right)^3\\
\left(\frac{1225}{1000}\right)^{\frac{1}{3}}&amp;=1 + \frac{r}{100}\\
\left(1.225\right)^{\frac{1}{3}}-1&amp;=\frac{r}{100}\\
\Rightarrow\qquad r&amp;=100\left(\left(1.225\right)^{\frac{1}{3}}-1\right)=\boxed{25}
\end{align*}

