Since we are dealing with $(a + b)(a + c)(b + c)$, consider the AM-GM inequality on each $(a + b)$, $(a + c)$, and $(b + c)$ individually:

\begin{align*}
(a + b) &\geq 2 \sqrt{ab}
\end{align*}
\begin{align*}
(a + c) &\geq 2 \sqrt{ac}
\end{align*}
\begin{align*}
(b + c) &\geq 2 \sqrt{bc}
\end{align*}

Using this fact, and considering the terms separately, we can now apply the Heavy-Am-Gm joint application:

\begin{align*}
(a + b)(a + c)(b + c) &\geq 8 \sqrt[3]{a^{2}b^{2 }c^{2}}
\end{align*}

We consider cubing the entire left side and right side. We get:

\begin{align*}
(a + b)(a + c)(b + c)  \geq (8 \sqrt[3]{a^{2}b^{2} c^{2}})^{3} \\
(a + b)(a + c)(b + c)  \geq 8^{3} a^{2} b^{2}c^{2}
\end{align*}

Divide both the left and right side of the entire expression by $abc$ to get:

\frac{(a + b)(a + c)(b + c)}{abc}\geq \frac{(8abc)^{3}}{abc} = \boxed{512}.

