\end{align*}
Note that we don't have a solution for k. In fact, there is no integer value for $k$, since this statement is false for all $k \in \mathbb{Z}$.
Thus $- 1 \equiv 0\pmod{20}$, which statement is clearly false for all integers. It should be quite obvious that
 \begin{align*}
(k+1)& \neq 30.
